{"parentUuid":"7d690b61-034f-4c34-af25-6970c96efad3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6b8557a2-9430-4f17-946a-1ea07dab5643","agentId":"aa14e9cc78e7c5b07","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XKAMXSaKf2xWAM4MKAVWZM","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nconcern: which module every piece of code belongs to\nsloprails: [file-guard/module-coverage, file-guard/module-distinct]\n# The code that must be mapped to modules.\nspace: [\"internal/**\", \"*-mock/**\"]\n# Globs of code not yet in any module. Each only shrinks.\nexceptions: []\n---\n\n# Every piece of code belongs to exactly one module\n\n## Concern\n\nWhich module owns each non-test Go file, so every concern has one home and no\ncode sits outside a boundary.\n\n## Decision\n\n- Every non-test Go file matching `space` lies in the `home` of exactly one\n  module (a `module.yaml`).\n- Module homes do not overlap.\n- Each module states its concern in the `concern:` line of its `module.yaml`.\n  No two modules' `concern:` lines name the same responsibility, whether\n  under different words or with one split across two modules.\n- A module's `home` holds only code of its `concern:`. A file belongs to\n  another concern when its main responsibility is what another module's\n  `concern:` line names.\n- Both are judged when a `module.yaml` is added or changed, against every\n  other module's `concern:`, `home` and the files each `home` glob matches.\n- Code matching `exceptions` belongs to no module; nothing new is added there.\n.sloprail/_lib/adr-conforms.md.j2\n.sloprail/_lib/adr.sh\n.sloprail/_lib/cells.sh\n.sloprail/_lib/changeset.sh\n.sloprail/_lib/confine.sh\n.sloprail/_lib/linked-adrs.sh\n.sloprail/_lib/modules.sh\n.sloprail/_lib/shape.sh\n.sloprail/_lib/snapshots.sh\n.sloprail/_lib/spec.sh\n.sloprail/_lib/subjects.sh\n.sloprail/config.yaml\n.sloprail/file-guard/adr-conformance/file-guard.yaml\n.sloprail/file-guard/adr-grounded/file-guard.yaml\n.sloprail/file-guard/adr-grounded/needs-words.sh\n.sloprail/file-guard/adr-grounded/prepare.sh\n.sloprail/file-guard/adr-grounded/subjects.sh\n.sloprail/file-guard/adr-grounded/words-ask-for-adr.md.j2\n.sloprail/file-guard/adr-linked/file-guard.yaml\n.sloprail/file-guard/adr-linked/links-resolve.sh\n.sloprail/file-guard/adr-matches-sloprails/file-guard.yaml\n.sloprail/file-guard/adr-matches-sloprails/prepare.sh\n.sloprail/file-guard/adr-matches-sloprails/rules-enforce-decision.md.j2\n.sloprail/file-guard/adr-matches-sloprails/subjects.sh\n.sloprail/file-guard/adr-well-formed/decision-is-sound.md.j2\n.sloprail/file-guard/adr-well-formed/file-guard.yaml\n.sloprail/file-guard/adr-well-formed/prepare.sh\n.sloprail/file-guard/capability-covered/covered.sh\n.sloprail/file-guard/capability-covered/file-guard.yaml\n.sloprail/file-guard/capability-grounded/added-or-removed.sh\ninternal/scenario/module.yaml:4:home: [\"internal/scenario/**\", \"claude-mock/internal/runner/runner.go\", \"claude-mock/internal/runner/runner_print.go\", \"claude-mock/internal/runner/config.go\", \"claude-mock/internal/runner/record*.go\", \"claude-mock/internal/runner/stream_scan.go\", \"claude-mock/main.go\", \"claude-mock/run.go\", \"claude-mock/run_flags.go\", \"claude-mock/e2etest/**\", \"codex-mock/main.go\", \"codex-mock/exec.go\", \"codex-mock/internal/runner/run.go\", \"codex-mock/internal/events/**\", \"cursor-mock/main.go\", \"cursor-mock/root.go\", \"cursor-mock/run.go\", \"cursor-mock/internal/runner/config.go\", \"cursor-mock/internal/runner/frames.go\"]   # everything about the concern lives here\ninternal/procexec/module.yaml:4:home: [\"internal/procexec/**\", \"claude-mock/internal/childenv/**\", \"codex-mock/internal/childenv/**\", \"cursor-mock/internal/childenv/**\"]   # everything about the concern lives here\ninternal/procexec/module.yaml:5:api: [\"internal/procexec\", \"claude-mock/internal/childenv\", \"codex-mock/internal/childenv\", \"cursor-mock/internal/childenv\"]       # the only packages others may import\ninternal/hooks/module.yaml:5:api: [\"internal/hooks\", \"claude-mock/internal/hooks\", \"codex-mock/internal/hooks\", \"cursor-mock/internal/hooks\"]      # the only packages others may import\ninternal/toolcall/module.yaml:4:home: [\"internal/toolcall/**\", \"claude-mock/internal/runner/stream_tool.go\", \"claude-mock/internal/runner/tool_hooks.go\", \"codex-mock/internal/runner/tool_host.go\", \"cursor-mock/internal/runner/toolhost.go\", \"cursor-mock/internal/runner/toolcall_frames.go\"]   # everything about the concern lives here\ninternal/transcript/module.yaml:4:home: [\"internal/transcript/**\", \"claude-mock/internal/runner/transcript*.go\", \"claude-mock/internal/runner/sessionwriter*.go\", \"cursor-mock/internal/runner/transcript.go\"]   # everything about the concern lives here\ninternal/tools/module.yaml:4:home: [\"internal/tools/**\", \"claude-mock/internal/toolexec/**\", \"claude-mock/internal/runner/schedulewakeup.go\", \"cursor-mock/internal/toolexec/**\"]   # everything about the concern lives here\ninternal/tools/module.yaml:5:api: [\"internal/tools\", \"claude-mock/internal/toolexec\", \"cursor-mock/internal/toolexec\"]       # the only packages others may import\ninternal/turnloop/module.yaml:4:home: [\"internal/turnloop/**\", \"claude-mock/internal/runner/stream.go\", \"claude-mock/internal/runner/stream_hook.go\", \"claude-mock/internal/runner/stream_turn.go\", \"codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go\", \"cursor-mock/internal/runner/run.go\", \"cursor-mock/internal/runner/host.go\"]   # everything about the concern lives here","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ec770174-52ed-445b-a14e-152e374e5ca6","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:53:17.296Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7d690b61-034f-4c34-af25-6970c96efad3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-aa14e9cc78e7c5b07","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513