{"parentUuid":"2b85b0f2-9fab-4ee6-a42d-7aadf105a8d0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"e3bd0840-a862-48c7-b928-fab715312060","agentId":"aa14e9cc78e7c5b07","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tq5YpX3pW8K3t4H68HKzpK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tstatement: >-\n2\t  A foreground shell command's result carries its output and a structured form\n3\t  of it; a command that exits non-zero is an error result carrying what the\n4\t  command printed and reporting its exit code (a harness may state the exit\n5\t  code only when the command printed nothing). (Where a harness knows that exit status 1 only reports\n6\t  no match or a difference (a search, a comparison), output limits, timeouts,\n7\t  what a command leaves behind for the next one, and commands run in the\n8\t  background are not part of this.)\n9\tproviders:\n10\t  claude:\n11\t    docs:\n12\t      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/tools-reference#bash-tool-behavior\n13\t    runs:\n14\t      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/bashfail\n15\t      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/stops\n16\t  codex:\n17\t    docs:\n18\t      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#posttooluse\n19\t    runs:\n20\t      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/shell-exit-status\n21\t    deviations:\n22\t      - adr: capability-grounding\n23\t        statement: >-\n24\t          Codex does not make a failed command an error result for the agent:\n25\t          what it is told is the command's output alone, the same text a\n26\t          success would have, with no exit code stated and none marked as an\n27\t          error (recorded: runs/shell-exit-status). The failure is shown only\n28\t          in the event stream's command_execution item, whose status is\n29\t          \"failed\" and whose exit_code and aggregated_output carry the exit\n30\t          status and what the command printed, and the mock does the same.\n31\t  cursor:\n32\t    docs:\n33\t      - https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#aftershellexecution\n34\