{"parentUuid":"41a76134-f738-42f2-bbcd-61877865d7b6","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa14e9cc78e7c5b07","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffaVnVLg1UrxpzBVLBKM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cursor is done and committed locally, but I have not pushed or opened a PR. The push gate (`verify-before-push`) blocks the push because `sr-checks` still shows three refusals.\n\nThose three refusals are about other capabilities' pairs. They appear to come from my small edits to shared files (`internal/tasks/command.go` and `task.go`, and `cursor-mock/internal/runner/run.go`), which make the judges re-judge those files' other markers:\n- `background-agent` / claude: the sub-agent `background: true` and agent-team variants are not covered by any test.\n- `background-bash` / claude: no test asserts the stream frames for a command that finishes on its own (the `midturn` run).\n- `session-start-hook` / cursor: the `continue:false` case has no test or run.\n\nNone of them touch this capability's pair, and all three held on the earlier runs as well. Clearing them would mean writing tests for claude and cursor behaviour outside my capability, so I stopped. You could waive the gate, or I could rework the shared-file edits to avoid triggering them.\n\nEverything for `foreground-subagent-bash-ends-with-response` passed the checks, and the cursor tests and `go build`/`go vet` pass.\n\n**Cursor: supported, with deviations**\n- **Recording:** `cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/foreground-subagent-bash-ends-with-response`. A foreground `Task` sub-agent starts a command with `block_until_ms:0`. The command is gone once the sub-agent answers, and the stream carries a `task_notification` with status `aborted`.\n- **Deviations:** the receipt is only `{shell_id,pid}` and does not say the command will be terminated (`capability-grounding`). The rest is `modeled-surface`: only a sub-agent's background shell is modelled, and the sub-agent runs from a mock-only `script` field.\n- **Mock code:** new `cursor-mock/internal/runner/background_shell.go` and `agent_task.go`. The only edits to existing code are:\n  - `run.go`: new `session` fields (`bg`, `owner`, `parent`, `shells`) and a `bg.Shutdown()` call\n  - `host.go`: `Tool` hands `Task` calls and sub-agent background shells to the new code\n  - `toolexec.go`: a `Background()` check for `block_until_ms:0`\n  - `internal/tasks` and `internal/procexec`: an additive `Pid` field and accessor so the receipt can carry the process id\n  - the `tasks` and `subagents` module homes now include the new cursor files\n- **Test:** `cursor-mock/e2e/002_scenario/subagent_shell_test.go`, marked `sr:proves foreground-subagent-bash-ends-with-response/cursor`.\n\n**Codex: unsupported**\n- **Evidence:** the recording is `codex-mock/snapshots/runs/foreground-subagent-bash-ends-with-response`. The sub-agent's backgrounded `sleep` was still running after the sub-agent finished, and there is no receipt. No mock code or markers.\n\nThe branch is `worktree-agent-aa14e9cc78e7c5b07`, rebased on `origin/main`. The spec cells are in `spec/capabilities/foreground-subagent-bash-ends-with-response.yaml`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1302,"cache_read_input_tokens":224591,"output_tokens":1193,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":84},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1302},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1193,"cache_read_input_tokens":224591,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1302,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1302,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cffa